[6] Insights
  * best method by MCC: Random forest (MCC 0.714, AUC 0.924)
  * the rule uses only 4 columns yet tracks the ensembles closely ->
    most of the signal is carried by a handful of clinical flags
  * tree ensembles can use interactions and graded features
    (Oldpeak, MaxHR) that the rule does not use
  * cleaning: cholesterol dropped; RestingBP=0 median-imputed; numerics winsorized -- all per training fold
  * per-fold SD describes variation across these folds;
    it does not establish statistical superiority or clinical readiness

